				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://publicneuro.eu/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">PublicnEUro is a repository for human brain-imaging research data, including MRI, PET, EEG, MEG and related data. It is operated by the Neurobiology Research Unit at Rigshospitalet, Region Hovedstaden, Denmark.

PublicnEUro supports both open and controlled access. Every published dataset receives a persistent identifier and a public catalogue record. Metadata remain openly available so that datasets can be discovered, evaluated and cited even when participant-level data require controlled access.

For controlled datasets, users are identified and must accept the dataset-specific Data User Agreement. Additional safeguards may apply to international transfers. This allows research data to be shared as openly as possible while protecting participants and respecting the requirements of the responsible data controller.</r3d:description>
